# CI artifact staging (night-zen-1 hotfix, the .auto-update leak
# class): the maintenance workflow's download-artifact step must land
# its staging directory outside the work tree (RUNNER_TEMP), but this
# ignore line is the second wall - an in-tree staging directory named
# .auto-update can never ride a commit even if a future edit moves
# the download back in-tree.
.auto-update/

# Python bytecode (night-dragon-maintenance-T1, the zelynic
# root-owned __pycache__ class): the interpreter writes caches beside
# imported sources with the invoking user's ownership; a root-run
# harness leaves root-owned .pyc files a later non-root teardown
# cannot remove. Ignored at both shapes - the directory and the
# bare file.
__pycache__/
__pycache__
*.pyc
